x86/pci: use ECAM before type 1 where there is one

raw_pci_read() and raw_pci_write() take configuration type 1 for domain 0
and registers below 256 whenever it exists, and ECAM only above. Under a
hypervisor type 1 is two traps per access - the address written to 0xcf8,
the data at 0xcfc - and on QEMU's q35 the 0xcf8 write cannot be coalesced:
the ICH9 reset control register at 0xcf9 splits the coalesced range, and
every one exits to userspace (1,496 per boot, measured 2026-09-29). ECAM is
one trap per access.

This kernel runs only in a VM whose ECAM covers every bus. Before MMCONFIG
is set up raw_pci_ext_ops is NULL and type 1 serves, as before.

Local patch for this machine: on real hardware type 1 is preferred for
reasons that do not apply here. Not upstream.

--- a/arch/x86/pci/common.c
+++ b/arch/x86/pci/common.c
@@ -40,20 +40,32 @@
 int raw_pci_read(unsigned int domain, unsigned int bus, unsigned int devfn,
 						int reg, int len, u32 *val)
 {
-	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
-		return raw_pci_ops->read(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	/*
+	 * ECAM first where there is one: an access through it is one trap to the
+	 * hypervisor, where type 1 is two - the write of the address to 0xcf8 and
+	 * the access at 0xcfc. This kernel runs only in a VM whose ECAM covers every
+	 * bus; before MMCONFIG is set up, raw_pci_ext_ops is NULL and type 1 serves.
+	 */
 	if (raw_pci_ext_ops)
 		return raw_pci_ext_ops->read(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
+		return raw_pci_ops->read(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
 int raw_pci_write(unsigned int domain, unsigned int bus, unsigned int devfn,
 						int reg, int len, u32 val)
 {
-	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
-		return raw_pci_ops->write(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	/*
+	 * ECAM first where there is one: an access through it is one trap to the
+	 * hypervisor, where type 1 is two - the write of the address to 0xcf8 and
+	 * the access at 0xcfc. This kernel runs only in a VM whose ECAM covers every
+	 * bus; before MMCONFIG is set up, raw_pci_ext_ops is NULL and type 1 serves.
+	 */
 	if (raw_pci_ext_ops)
 		return raw_pci_ext_ops->write(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
+	if (domain == 0 && reg < 256 && raw_pci_ops)
+		return raw_pci_ops->write(domain, bus, devfn, reg, len, val);
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
